[{:db/id "q-52200/selection/ee6c990a784c74ec124e6a9c6249f2121fad0829d8ec7dbe53ba1da07f491da1" :answer/id #uuid "1df6e996-fa00-5ebd-8182-593f4d0645d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=5,\\,w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200/selection/622b4e04c717b22c44ac6e0b76f15dd2a3aad7002460419197acbb846b57e6b0" :answer/id #uuid "a4c685e2-4e75-535f-8f2d-5cfd3706d5f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=\\frac{1}{2},\\,w=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200/selection/12965f47922a8f24beec407c7d9f6fb7f5b96d39572b8e8292ed4610914df0b8" :answer/id #uuid "2c6cf477-5ce2-54f4-959c-7a8b0448196c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=5,\\,w=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200/selection/b911c5bce7a4b6a061fcbae6444788384c885fd32951aaf481d30fc0f5bdfccf" :answer/id #uuid "7644c12c-ffc7-5139-aadf-8a50bca98fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=6,\\,w=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200/selection/504d4430921c93e2d23d91bd785461d4fbb64c60462552e36b0b61db28d71cef" :answer/id #uuid "de0c61b5-0807-5f50-8201-7b875f7b4a0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=1,\\,w=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60880ebc-476c-595d-ad75-495f4c1eaea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-52200/selection/ee6c990a784c74ec124e6a9c6249f2121fad0829d8ec7dbe53ba1da07f491da1" :answer-field/choices ["q-52200/selection/ee6c990a784c74ec124e6a9c6249f2121fad0829d8ec7dbe53ba1da07f491da1" "q-52200/selection/622b4e04c717b22c44ac6e0b76f15dd2a3aad7002460419197acbb846b57e6b0" "q-52200/selection/12965f47922a8f24beec407c7d9f6fb7f5b96d39572b8e8292ed4610914df0b8" "q-52200/selection/b911c5bce7a4b6a061fcbae6444788384c885fd32951aaf481d30fc0f5bdfccf" "q-52200/selection/504d4430921c93e2d23d91bd785461d4fbb64c60462552e36b0b61db28d71cef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-52200" :question/id #uuid "9e136b8d-f97f-56d2-a8c3-ae7a8f77031b" :question/math-academy-id "q-52200" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2v+3w=10 \\\\ v-\\frac{3}{4}w=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $4.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2v+3w=10 \\\\ v-\\frac{3}{4}w=5 & |\\,\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2v+3w=10 \\\\ 4v-3w=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $3w$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-3w$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $w$-variable, and allows us to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+\\cancel{3w} & =10 \\\\ 4v-\\cancel{3w} & =20 \\\\ 6v & =30 \\\\ v & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $v=5$ into the equation $4v-3w=20$ to solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4v-3w & =20 \\\\ 4\\cdot 5-3w & =20 \\\\ 20-3w & =20 \\\\ -3w & =0 \\\\ w & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $v=5$ and $w=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-52200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-52200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b2701b96-8c48-5e59-8e22-0700a85feb13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "38031efc-c416-5439-8c0b-7c1d67f23c99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2fa9c7-cdcf-5e1d-bde2-0964c62f4ef1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216037/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-216037/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-216037/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c5c44155-0f2e-59ba-be7c-8a7c1f96b015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "08f3bfb3-9a73-59af-96b0-e84c0a9b7362" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216037/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-216037/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216037" :question/id #uuid "ffd5bd9a-1589-5f50-ab84-6ad9ec3a97cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-216037" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+2b=5 \\\\ -3a+8b=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $4.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+2b=5 & |\\,\\times 4 \\\\ -3a+8b=-4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3a+8b=20 \\\\ -3a+8b=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $3a$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-3a$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $a$-variable, and allows us to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3a}+8b & =20 \\\\ -\\cancel{3a}+8b & =-4 \\\\ 16b & =16 \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $b=1$ into the equation $-3a+8b=-4$ to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+8b & =-4 \\\\ -3a+8\\cdot 1 & =-4 \\\\ -3a+8 & =-4 \\\\ -3a & =-12 \\\\ a & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=4$ and $b=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216037/field-1" "q-216037/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216075/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "216262a7-20f5-5120-b25a-369da1cc8db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216075/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2c8284c-97cb-52d4-ad50-7cf979c81b30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216075/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-216075/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216075/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c5a3923f-a19d-5b89-a311-b6504e803f15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216075/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3fa289ca-997f-5f40-ab58-519a72ce3113" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216075/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-216075/field-2/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216075" :question/id #uuid "92d72b3d-3f0b-503b-a282-400f532d2a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-216075" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5p+q=3 \\\\ 6p-\\frac{1}{4}q=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $4.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5p+q=3 \\\\ 6p-\\frac{1}{4}q=-8 & |\\,\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5p+q=3 \\\\ 24p-q=-32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $q$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-q$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $q$-variable, and allows us to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+\\cancel{q} & =3 \\\\ 24p-\\cancel{q} & =-32 \\\\ 29p & =-29 \\\\ p & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $p=-1$ into the equation $5p+q=3$ to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+q & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-1)+q & =3 \\\\ -5+q & =3 \\\\ q & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-1,\\,q=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216075/field-1" "q-216075/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection/0ccebafe55084a96d64ee98d6a031022da2e5fceee14405b0da572035a292bfe" :answer/id #uuid "3bba6eef-b620-5c41-a7aa-66bcd70416e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=3,\\,q=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection/74270f6d327e7fb3fc9f2458638977fa0c00cf1140501b2356556e88c5bd945e" :answer/id #uuid "4e7bf387-a643-5ae7-ac34-ee18d4d3667f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=3,\\,q=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection/7a1d50f9ea6936d27080bb6d3c36b6693454c97c01c7a9d9cee95725526ef3d8" :answer/id #uuid "8e0f0fac-a601-5316-b6b7-9ece41f2fb4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=5,\\,q=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection/dcb90233a5ceb6476a7cf022ac9632386d97e6fca28768fbfb6d8ac8970ae304" :answer/id #uuid "7700ac3f-544e-5951-aa38-4a393d6ed87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-3,\\,q=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection/b7a6bb92f1241c6311685768c04a54263b34d8fb2f741774b4f86e192c9827db" :answer/id #uuid "6e169c4f-fa97-59ce-9197-f637dce1bc9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=9,\\,q=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd7d036-c3b3-5aa0-af10-0828094c3b7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216042/selection/74270f6d327e7fb3fc9f2458638977fa0c00cf1140501b2356556e88c5bd945e" :answer-field/choices ["q-216042/selection/0ccebafe55084a96d64ee98d6a031022da2e5fceee14405b0da572035a292bfe" "q-216042/selection/74270f6d327e7fb3fc9f2458638977fa0c00cf1140501b2356556e88c5bd945e" "q-216042/selection/7a1d50f9ea6936d27080bb6d3c36b6693454c97c01c7a9d9cee95725526ef3d8" "q-216042/selection/dcb90233a5ceb6476a7cf022ac9632386d97e6fca28768fbfb6d8ac8970ae304" "q-216042/selection/b7a6bb92f1241c6311685768c04a54263b34d8fb2f741774b4f86e192c9827db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216042" :question/id #uuid "92288a0c-f633-5c57-b73b-6161a16e5a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-216042" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3p+\\frac{4}{5}q=-1 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $5.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3p+\\frac{4}{5}q=-1 & |\\,\\times 5 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-15p+4q=-5 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $4q$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-4q$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $q$-variable, and allows us to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15p+\\cancel{4q} & =-5 \\\\ 9p-\\cancel{4q} & =-13 \\\\ -6p & =-18 \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $p=3$ into the equation $9p-4q=-13$ to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9p-4q & =-13 \\\\ 9\\cdot 3-4q & =-13 \\\\ 27-4q & =-13 \\\\ -4q & =-40 \\\\ q & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=3,\\,q=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection/a6c7bf975bf9bcd19d762511c7df1262f3e3984d23d69db9cc484a72d6cee91f" :answer/id #uuid "ac6e0ebb-4fbf-594e-8e5d-4d7663863709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection/0f0d5208509248bc41441c1bbf04961f62d6c9a2e9d1b35e3bfdb34cbdf9e855" :answer/id #uuid "cef8c113-0295-52ea-9e70-1c1a65fe5937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\,y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection/f40a3aae0626a05598952b50e3e622f4516d1bf16038f681daf9c44b05fbcfe1" :answer/id #uuid "d8dceb62-ce6f-57f8-aa91-be87b574b8f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection/c7fd09528b860e68067102a4edb439dab795f73bd586834f186b9c6be4e3957a" :answer/id #uuid "9c5bd586-fee3-5b90-a97c-a4ac034e7731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=6,\\,y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection/a1124fc5928ff2befb15bc02893cc6433db38864a62996b667551b6a07d4529b" :answer/id #uuid "ccfc0f0f-f464-57d7-9c43-fbe4849602a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=6,\\,y=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6751d96-4863-5fef-bf8c-4e8837e454e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216049/selection/c7fd09528b860e68067102a4edb439dab795f73bd586834f186b9c6be4e3957a" :answer-field/choices ["q-216049/selection/a6c7bf975bf9bcd19d762511c7df1262f3e3984d23d69db9cc484a72d6cee91f" "q-216049/selection/0f0d5208509248bc41441c1bbf04961f62d6c9a2e9d1b35e3bfdb34cbdf9e855" "q-216049/selection/f40a3aae0626a05598952b50e3e622f4516d1bf16038f681daf9c44b05fbcfe1" "q-216049/selection/c7fd09528b860e68067102a4edb439dab795f73bd586834f186b9c6be4e3957a" "q-216049/selection/a1124fc5928ff2befb15bc02893cc6433db38864a62996b667551b6a07d4529b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216049" :question/id #uuid "7031c3ac-9f5c-549e-a734-1e40943152a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216049" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x-9y=-12 \\\\ \\frac{5}{6}x-2y=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x-9y=-12 \\\\ \\frac{5}{6}x-2y=9 & |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5x-9y=-12 \\\\ 5x-12y=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $-5x$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $5x$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5x}-9y & =-12 \\\\ \\cancel{5x}-12y & =54 \\\\ -21y & =42 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-2$ into the equation $-5x-9y=-12$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x-9y & =-12 \\\\ -5x-9\\cdot (-2) & =-12 \\\\ -5x+18 & =-12 \\\\ -5x & =-30 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216049/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14370371-529b-5f25-9963-62c0cd9a172e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection/4fe18a76ae40b30b9a9de86e3308dc4ecb01563afa12d9b73d84cb2981686778" :answer/id #uuid "d5b2acee-6697-5d93-8d8d-13565f1017c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,y=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection/3a5955ef16f28903cef7cf51afaa168ab12bfc7877aa233de7b01e1d146b4676" :answer/id #uuid "4c3afc8e-03c7-57ee-8f67-a0ffee7c4270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,y=-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection/01e3d55fad36b415ee38766ed82001e5359ce6df77adf737f13619c635568f4d" :answer/id #uuid "50b03ae3-1445-5c9c-9e58-b705b006b72d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,y=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection/85108097a0fb8c595aa6831c205ff2fd88616b106e68f5fb2ae49c6583bfd191" :answer/id #uuid "17b4c048-4ff1-5569-a7bf-acfa129e2da3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection/da4dac99a50d86bd63c77defeb019f8c4b33edac3febd052e46c970c10b644cf" :answer/id #uuid "d633e03f-6c9f-5d7e-b7b0-d5a739ca76b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7eab116e-7fd3-5f6d-9c61-4b026cc745b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75862/selection/85108097a0fb8c595aa6831c205ff2fd88616b106e68f5fb2ae49c6583bfd191" :answer-field/choices ["q-75862/selection/4fe18a76ae40b30b9a9de86e3308dc4ecb01563afa12d9b73d84cb2981686778" "q-75862/selection/3a5955ef16f28903cef7cf51afaa168ab12bfc7877aa233de7b01e1d146b4676" "q-75862/selection/01e3d55fad36b415ee38766ed82001e5359ce6df77adf737f13619c635568f4d" "q-75862/selection/85108097a0fb8c595aa6831c205ff2fd88616b106e68f5fb2ae49c6583bfd191" "q-75862/selection/da4dac99a50d86bd63c77defeb019f8c4b33edac3febd052e46c970c10b644cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75862" :question/id #uuid "7cd25c8c-eb40-551c-be66-2948be61be80" :question/math-academy-id "q-75862" :question/problem "Find the solution to the  following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{1}{3}y=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{1}{3}y=2 & |\\times 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=1 & |\\times 4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=6 \\\\ 2x-y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the second equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $y$ term that can cancel with the $-y$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=6 &  \\\\ 2x-y=4 & |\\,\\times (-1)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=6 \\\\ -2x+y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable, and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-\\cancel{y} & =6 \\\\ -2x+\\cancel{y} & =-4 \\\\ (6x-2x) & =(6-4) \\\\ 4x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the second equation to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & =4 \\\\ 2(\\frac{1}{2})-y & =4 \\\\ 1-y & =4 \\\\ y & =1-4 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection/20a61cba450bd0266c5afa5531c190c3255b98f0b2b95a2240ce33103af6a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "1d010d9d-f4ee-591e-9d8d-1ab1bf3029da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=6,\\,b=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection/8496d0c212e82fd1e947fa347020d56c3b5a06dd612d9ebb44c14636c5d0663a" :answer/id #uuid "07480345-aec5-5c4e-a528-0c35344d7771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=8,\\,b=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection/4b1a848a9f4786b1a196880cf8ba17c901da0856e30055c792c9d34947ba4fa4" :answer/id #uuid "13a2a89b-0eb5-5afa-b7e8-35a5ffc87a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-8,\\,b=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection/f7194e81ecb0ba661dfedbb714c140837c99c99e1fa47c692dbc3ca3b7676b74" :answer/id #uuid "9179a10a-62ff-52f6-b1c2-6f6d01375428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection/b948493583ce9d4eb0ffbe3395db3a05961477100b2326c3ab9b5f4c88869e86" :answer/id #uuid "14fa8223-3e30-57d8-abd9-a52e0c4a7a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0b6550-4b96-5988-ba37-4ab11834de74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216309/selection/4b1a848a9f4786b1a196880cf8ba17c901da0856e30055c792c9d34947ba4fa4" :answer-field/choices ["q-216309/selection/20a61cba450bd0266c5afa5531c190c3255b98f0b2b95a2240ce33103af6a9ce" "q-216309/selection/8496d0c212e82fd1e947fa347020d56c3b5a06dd612d9ebb44c14636c5d0663a" "q-216309/selection/4b1a848a9f4786b1a196880cf8ba17c901da0856e30055c792c9d34947ba4fa4" "q-216309/selection/f7194e81ecb0ba661dfedbb714c140837c99c99e1fa47c692dbc3ca3b7676b74" "q-216309/selection/b948493583ce9d4eb0ffbe3395db3a05961477100b2326c3ab9b5f4c88869e86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216309" :question/id #uuid "6f83cc86-a896-545c-8edd-a31db10e015a" :question/math-academy-id "q-216309" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+b=-3 \\\\ a-\\frac{1}{3}b=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}a+b=-3 & |\\times 4 \\\\ a-\\frac{1}{3}b=-9 & |\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3a+4b=-12 \\\\ 3a-b=-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-3a$ term that can cancel with the $3a$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+4b=-12 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 3a-b=-27 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-3a-4b=12 \\\\ 3a-b=-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $a$-variable, and allows us to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{3a}-4b & =12 \\\\ \\cancel{3a}-b & =-27 \\\\ (-4b-b) & =(12-27) \\\\ -5b & =-15 \\\\ b & =\\frac{-15}{-5} \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $b=3$ into the second equation to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-b & =-27 \\\\ 3a-3 & =-27 \\\\ 3a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{24}{3} \\\\ a & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=-8,\\,b=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-216309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection/ee6c990a784c74ec124e6a9c6249f2121fad0829d8ec7dbe53ba1da07f491da1" :answer/id #uuid "9e6a5dd7-f9cc-5799-9258-14f47a54b6e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=5,\\,w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection/01f86188bcb1b31824300be0640d528d3e7a1a99d3739f8d7fc19ce4e7c6c298" :answer/id #uuid "4f639cd4-b5c0-5f11-9565-51a95891e8a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=-3,\\,w=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection/b865b49e9e61d3aa0fa5e3a0097d1b1ceccf91185de5d754f951d56960c172a1" :answer/id #uuid "cb8f5e21-9228-5b72-b044-dc8b0ac3b08e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=3,\\,w=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection/ed9c649e3b7fdeafc4f93f4d1472042bf3ac515211552a220b054daa266600ad" :answer/id #uuid "541d2208-700b-55e9-9792-2e7d10cc9bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=-3,\\,w=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection/725de6e1b12a96ae7e8495944bbab6ed35aa5c82ca37fea6d998f83bc014556a" :answer/id #uuid "9bdca147-cf66-5649-a213-77c1ddb68193" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=4,\\,w=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd628f1a-2548-51f4-869f-7589a6eda7be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-52202/selection/ed9c649e3b7fdeafc4f93f4d1472042bf3ac515211552a220b054daa266600ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-52202/selection/ee6c990a784c74ec124e6a9c6249f2121fad0829d8ec7dbe53ba1da07f491da1" "q-52202/selection/01f86188bcb1b31824300be0640d528d3e7a1a99d3739f8d7fc19ce4e7c6c298" "q-52202/selection/b865b49e9e61d3aa0fa5e3a0097d1b1ceccf91185de5d754f951d56960c172a1" "q-52202/selection/ed9c649e3b7fdeafc4f93f4d1472042bf3ac515211552a220b054daa266600ad" "q-52202/selection/725de6e1b12a96ae7e8495944bbab6ed35aa5c82ca37fea6d998f83bc014556a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-52202" :question/id #uuid "1145ce5a-6b11-53ed-9fcc-76e83be7ade1" :question/math-academy-id "q-52202" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}v-2w=5 \\\\ -v-\\frac{2}{5}w=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}v-2w=5 & |\\times 3 \\\\ -v-\\frac{2}{5}w=5 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5v-6w=15 \\\\ -5v-2w=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $v$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{5v}-6w & =15 \\\\ -\\cancel{5v}-2w & =25 \\\\ (-6w-2w) & =(15+25) \\\\ -8w & =40 \\\\ w & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $w=-5$ into the first equation to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-6w & =15 \\\\ 5v-6(-5) & =15 \\\\ 5v+30 & =15 \\\\ 5v & =-15 \\\\ v & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $v=-3,\\,w=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-52202/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-52202"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-216178"] :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}a+3b=-6 & |\\times 2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}a-\\frac{1}{3}b=9 & |\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5a+6b=-12 \\\\ 5a-b=27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $a$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5a}+6b & =-12 \\\\ \\cancel{5a}-b & =27 \\\\ (6b-b) & =(-12+27) \\\\ 5b & =15 \\\\ b & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $b=3$ into the second equation to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-b & =27 \\\\ 5a-3 & =27 \\\\ 5a & =30 \\\\ a & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=6,\\,b=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-216199/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "ad0370a2-f291-5c05-8fcb-55081034cdae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216199/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9d7af9-b3e4-533e-a7e9-3b85602e7f17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216199/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-216199/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216199/field-2/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "e5ac7636-c5bd-58a8-a375-1daa5b3c2995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216199/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcca4943-105b-5ffd-83e6-1d85660f411c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216199/field-2/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer-field/choices ["q-216199/field-2/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216199" :question/id #uuid "fcdf7481-e9da-5b94-b4eb-a65b1ffb01f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-216199" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a-\\frac{5}{4}b=30 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}a+b=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a-\\frac{5}{4}b=30 & |\\times 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}a+b=-6 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}8a-5b=120 \\\\ a+5b=-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $b$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8a-\\cancel{5b} & =120 \\\\ a+\\cancel{5b} & =-30 \\\\ (8a+a) & =(120-30) \\\\ 9a & =90 \\\\ a & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=10$ into the second equation to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+5b & =-30 \\\\ 10+5b & =-30 \\\\ 5b & =-40 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{40}{5} \\\\ b & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=10,\\,b=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216199/field-1" "q-216199/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215839/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "635c3d4e-cea3-5564-bf97-114681db564d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215839/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1616e885-2265-5e87-b6b4-eb4d6fa72228" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215839/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-215839/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215839/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "8ca439ac-c3f8-5a03-991a-66dba31344f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215839/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7320e5d-faf3-531d-a384-17aabb8d1165" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215839/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-215839/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215839" :question/id #uuid "ffb18301-b485-5f96-b6f9-5a55c54a6ed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-215839" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2s+t=7 \\\\ \\frac{3s}{8}+\\frac{t}{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,t=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $8.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2s+t=7 \\\\ \\frac{3s}{8}+\\frac{t}{2}=1 & |\\,\\times 8\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2s+t=7 \\\\ 3s+4t=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $t$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2s+t & =7 \\\\ t & =7-2s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $t=7-2s$ into the second equation and solve for $s:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3s+4t & =8 \\\\ 3s+4(7-2s) & =8 \\\\ 3s+28-8s & =8 \\\\ -5s+28 & =8 \\\\ -5s & =-20 \\\\ s & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $t,$ we substitute $s=4$ into the equation $t=7-2s,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =7-2s \\\\  & =7-2(4) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=4,\\,t=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-215839/field-1" "q-215839/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215839"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection/5f0721aa6b3f86675d0946a4ea7909c51b6d479387ed895434a0fa3731ed4c86" :answer/id #uuid "a7594cdc-5fca-519d-baa8-7cd8f381d612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection/da4dac99a50d86bd63c77defeb019f8c4b33edac3febd052e46c970c10b644cf" :answer/id #uuid "bb3de9f5-1e0e-5678-a1a9-6ad59daf10f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection/f6a9a29b576effed35cf8cd3d7c75be15bca9c306f1c649e33ceada27be00754" :answer/id #uuid "1a8cc5a2-98d3-552e-830d-ea43611ee8f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection/3644ab7e18372cab12b74059c6d13c687cfa5e3327c743116081b3156a0d0b2c" :answer/id #uuid "3e63e066-2f8b-5d34-ac78-0c2587880309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,\\,y=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection/372b54c2f92a19c9ff759c4ec80d94cf8bf026fedc71d94708cb875952431dc1" :answer/id #uuid "89fea6f1-2c25-5086-84ab-0beebc533fe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\,y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcf1598-e93b-50fb-9d77-1ca3089bc11c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-26094/selection/5f0721aa6b3f86675d0946a4ea7909c51b6d479387ed895434a0fa3731ed4c86" :answer-field/choices ["q-26094/selection/5f0721aa6b3f86675d0946a4ea7909c51b6d479387ed895434a0fa3731ed4c86" "q-26094/selection/da4dac99a50d86bd63c77defeb019f8c4b33edac3febd052e46c970c10b644cf" "q-26094/selection/f6a9a29b576effed35cf8cd3d7c75be15bca9c306f1c649e33ceada27be00754" "q-26094/selection/3644ab7e18372cab12b74059c6d13c687cfa5e3327c743116081b3156a0d0b2c" "q-26094/selection/372b54c2f92a19c9ff759c4ec80d94cf8bf026fedc71d94708cb875952431dc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-26094" :question/id #uuid "a438562b-561a-5a07-8688-ac5551c46746" :question/math-academy-id "q-26094" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5y}{6}-2=0 \\\\ 3x+y+6=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5y}{6}-2=0 & |\\,\\times 6 \\\\ 3x+y+6=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-12=0 \\\\ 3x+y+6=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the second equation can easily be solved for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y+6 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $y=-3x-6$ into the first equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y-12 & =0 \\\\ x+5(-3x-6)-12 & =0 \\\\ x-15x-30-12 & =0 \\\\ -14x-42 & =0 \\\\ -14x & =42 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $y,$ we substitute $x=-3$ into the equation $y=-3x-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x-6 \\\\  & =-3(-3)-6 \\\\  & =9-6 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-26094/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-26094"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection/caca7ef4b8ac49880a8bb9efdc80a94532c4b57d7d9f55d267afdbc2d737a878" :answer/id #uuid "df689d00-8d5c-5e2f-a8c7-6288497218ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,\\,y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection/1659dd14cc6f5f6c03763d77c912eece31d9bba90de16e100d3439b366be23c3" :answer/id #uuid "86e271e2-fbd8-5c4a-aa46-e807b51319e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection/773e181f557e08fe8fd96b1d35e5f9eca6b9909adf02dfbe0ed57edecbb08bb8" :answer/id #uuid "4271c9de-f6a5-5131-9a28-e2b014bf1bfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection/991aef0df75b6bcbbde3498a51f4620a66243188d86752d6c431cc57f462145d" :answer/id #uuid "2adec1c1-fa80-5c3e-8c1a-fcb7f93bbe03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection/effb7bfef35fc2ddfdddbc06653fbcdd914b81b90f49e9e40e3954ed8676d173" :answer/id #uuid "f0325724-fd68-59cb-b098-66d7c2163809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\,y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c49f84c3-cdd1-5252-983a-ac70cd4e2946" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-215824/selection/773e181f557e08fe8fd96b1d35e5f9eca6b9909adf02dfbe0ed57edecbb08bb8" :answer-field/choices ["q-215824/selection/caca7ef4b8ac49880a8bb9efdc80a94532c4b57d7d9f55d267afdbc2d737a878" "q-215824/selection/1659dd14cc6f5f6c03763d77c912eece31d9bba90de16e100d3439b366be23c3" "q-215824/selection/773e181f557e08fe8fd96b1d35e5f9eca6b9909adf02dfbe0ed57edecbb08bb8" "q-215824/selection/991aef0df75b6bcbbde3498a51f4620a66243188d86752d6c431cc57f462145d" "q-215824/selection/effb7bfef35fc2ddfdddbc06653fbcdd914b81b90f49e9e40e3954ed8676d173"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215824" :question/id #uuid "b79f1980-1979-56f6-9b8c-7d297f6d53ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-215824" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{7}+\\frac{2y}{7}=1 \\\\ x-y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $7.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{7}+\\frac{2y}{7}=1 & |\\,\\times 7 \\\\ x-y=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=7 \\\\ x-y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & =1 \\\\ x & =1+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=1+y$ into the first equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =7 \\\\ (1+y)+2y & =7 \\\\ 1+3y & =7 \\\\ 3y & =6 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=2$ into the equation $x=1+y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1+y \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3,\\,y=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d28675b3-ec2b-5200-956e-5000f5aec7e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0fd05fa3-73b8-5bf6-84e3-a1ba006e1ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "df61b658-6a58-5152-81a9-1c00ceec6a21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215827/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-215827/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-215827/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "49079722-f69c-5424-b1d3-17711195c7be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0596d75-fb40-5098-87cf-f2606e19f069" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215827/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-215827/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215827" :question/id #uuid "4fcca4f2-b904-5b28-bf28-2efe9e3d955f" :question/math-academy-id "q-215827" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a-b=7 \\\\ \\frac{a}{5}-\\frac{2b}{5}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $5.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a-b=7 \\\\ \\frac{a}{5}-\\frac{2b}{5}=1 & |\\,\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2a-b=7 \\\\ a-2b=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $a$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-2b & =5 \\\\ a & =5+2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $a=5+2b$ into the first equation and solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-b & =7 \\\\ 2(5+2b)-b & =7 \\\\ 10+4b-b & =7 \\\\ 3b & =-3 \\\\ b & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $a,$ we substitute $b=-1$ into the equation $a=5+2b,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =5+2b \\\\  & =5+2(-1) \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3,\\,b=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215827/field-1" "q-215827/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215827"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215738/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "d43b0e35-5a7e-5387-b7f4-707b5aa5b6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215738/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "56f49e56-d8f9-557f-9b51-c2db7f8ba804" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215738/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer-field/choices ["q-215738/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215738/field-2/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer/id #uuid "6c888562-a37b-5aeb-a2e3-b0df5d06c22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215738/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a0814d-7540-5f9d-bf7d-276819200557" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215738/field-2/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer-field/choices ["q-215738/field-2/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215738" :question/id #uuid "81946f52-f39d-57ab-a887-d387ae9bede6" :question/math-academy-id "q-215738" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q=-6 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{2}+\\frac{5q}{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $2.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q=-6 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{2}+\\frac{5q}{2}=2 & |\\,\\times 2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2p+4q=-6 \\\\ 3p+5q=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $p$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p+4q & =-6 \\\\ 2p & =-4q-6 \\\\ p & =-2q-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $p=-2q-3$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p+5q & =4 \\\\ 3(-2q-3)+5q & =4 \\\\ -6q-9+5q & =4 \\\\ -q & =13 \\\\ q & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to find the value of $p,$ we substitute $q=-13$ into the equation $p=-2q-3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =-2q-3 \\\\  & =-2(-13)-3 \\\\  & =26-3 \\\\  & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=23,\\,q=-13.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215738/field-1" "q-215738/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection/de323713e4e9c5144d79cf5a6c60510b69c5aff590e39ee53338b6411eb559bb" :answer/id #uuid "56da5624-b584-5144-b0cd-ad4780a04f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection/775f5e7e89066b96baa444ae8965e46ab5dc09f46fd71b9054cd088a0b1428b0" :answer/id #uuid "4b8bda0f-5b8d-5b38-8bb8-9bddf729c0fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,\\,y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection/85144751def5776dac86284afcc9781bb96c67182d8e379c9a6a5d658cb25848" :answer/id #uuid "553c5845-1ba4-5783-8959-1201ea7a4579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection/8ccf53ec71963c9d5b9973883a8d23f64cc17c64b1a0e03840c20ad18136acec" :answer/id #uuid "ab70aeca-77c5-5204-ac3b-258559625507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\,y=-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection/4a5cd878e46f03dfefea4a749c7d4edb9dc26eaa2064a08651e4eb0f1c756b8a" :answer/id #uuid "c707d476-d48d-5a31-83e0-d14ca6585762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc7fd1a2-4f2c-5595-93ee-d748093f560d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216059/selection/de323713e4e9c5144d79cf5a6c60510b69c5aff590e39ee53338b6411eb559bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-216059/selection/de323713e4e9c5144d79cf5a6c60510b69c5aff590e39ee53338b6411eb559bb" "q-216059/selection/775f5e7e89066b96baa444ae8965e46ab5dc09f46fd71b9054cd088a0b1428b0" "q-216059/selection/85144751def5776dac86284afcc9781bb96c67182d8e379c9a6a5d658cb25848" "q-216059/selection/8ccf53ec71963c9d5b9973883a8d23f64cc17c64b1a0e03840c20ad18136acec" "q-216059/selection/4a5cd878e46f03dfefea4a749c7d4edb9dc26eaa2064a08651e4eb0f1c756b8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216059" :question/id #uuid "e810c346-0f80-58b2-8a40-15d2db43a85d" :question/math-academy-id "q-216059" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{1}{3}y=-1 \\\\ x+\\frac{3}{7}y=\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{1}{3}y=-1 & |\\times 3 \\\\ x+\\frac{3}{7}y=\\frac{1}{7} & |\\times 7\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4x+y=-3 \\\\ 7x+3y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+y & =-3 \\\\ y & =-3-4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $y=-3-4x$ into the second equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+3y & =1 \\\\ 7x+3(-3-4x) & =1 \\\\ 7x-9-12x & =1 \\\\ -5x & =10 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $y,$ we substitute $x=-2$ into the equation $y=-3-4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3-4x \\\\  & =-3-4(-2) \\\\  & =-3+8 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2$ and $y=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "098cfbd9-b1ee-516b-b2ea-5e70d08dd8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d74553d7-b1fa-550d-bca5-fa8671c27b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd45a38b-1ad9-5c8c-ab73-bffbf5c0f632" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215849/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-215849/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-215849/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "88ada8fe-3b8f-56c4-8cdb-a9aa7cfa0550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b470abb-2feb-5634-abbc-96081f32da5c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215849/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-215849/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215849" :question/id #uuid "7cfbe2ec-3385-5eae-80b7-ab6a0cfc8ffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-215849" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{5}y=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 2x-\\frac{1}{2}y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $5$ and the second equation by $2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{5}y=\\frac{1}{5} & |\\,\\times 5 \\\\ 2x-\\frac{1}{2}y=1 & |\\,\\times 2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=1 \\\\ 4x-y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Solving for $y$ in the second equation we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =2 \\\\ -y & =-4x+2 \\\\ y & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=4x-2$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y & =1 \\\\ 5x-2(4x-2) & =1 \\\\ 5x-8x+4 & =1 \\\\ -3x+4 & =1 \\\\ -3x & =-3 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we substitute $x=1$ into the equation $y=4x-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4x-2 \\\\  & =4(1)-2 \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=1,\\,y=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215849/field-1" "q-215849/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215856/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "08af4282-6c1f-5ead-a2f7-3f60bf01edfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215856/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a61997b0-5df8-5fa7-8284-936c954aa008" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215856/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-215856/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215856/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "05216356-4221-5c52-b37c-391394706db7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215856/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "915186b8-6215-5ebb-935e-9dee0123a0bf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215856/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-215856/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215856" :question/id #uuid "3ca740a3-72d4-5cec-bd44-d4347f714dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-215856" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3}y=2 \\\\ x+\\frac{4}{7}y=-\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3}y=2 & |\\times 3 \\\\ x+\\frac{4}{7}y=-\\frac{3}{7} & |\\times 7\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+7y=6 \\\\ 7x+4y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+7y & =6 \\\\ x & =6-7y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=6-7y$ into the second equation and then solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+4y & =-3 \\\\ 7(6-7y)+4y & =-3 \\\\ 42-49y+4y & =-3 \\\\ -45y & =-45 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation $x=6-7y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6-7y\\text{ } \\\\  & =6-7(1) \\\\  & =6-7 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1$ and $y=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215856/field-1" "q-215856/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215856"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066/field-1/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "3ad329c1-6776-5fe7-8330-4c38a259ab06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4558fc9b-97c8-5cae-a42a-27d235f80e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c3e29aa-2b80-5f6a-a7a9-21580c2118ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216066/field-1/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer-field/choices ["q-216066/field-1/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-216066/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "5dd76742-e5ea-5b04-9764-2bbf88e7df59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8c8a47-a4f2-5cef-8f1e-6918ac36e4a3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-216066/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-216066/field-2/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216066" :question/id #uuid "7c1fa185-fc78-508c-827a-049d99108d0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-216066" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{6}v-\\frac{1}{6}w=2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}v+\\frac{1}{5}w=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$v=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,w=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $6$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{6}v-\\frac{1}{6}w=2 & |\\times 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}v+\\frac{1}{5}w=2 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4v-w=12 \\\\ 2v+w=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the second equation can easily be solved for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+w & =10 \\\\ w & =10-2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $w=10-2v$ into the first equation and then solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4v-w & =12 \\\\ 4v-(10-2v) & =12 \\\\ 4v-10+2v & =12 \\\\ 6v & =22 \\\\ v & =\\frac{22}{6} \\\\ v & =\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $w,$ we substitute $v=\\frac{11}{3}$ into the equation $w=10-2v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =10-2v\\text{ } \\\\  & =10-2(\\frac{11}{3}) \\\\  & =10-\\frac{22}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-22}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $v=\\frac{11}{3}$ and $w=\\frac{8}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216066/field-1" "q-216066/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection/1cdb79a815d8131b9bb3ea2d69f4bf518d6d419b61574ce7ce45e2877b717e2a" :answer/id #uuid "6e62da2e-fe3d-5b86-becc-1af1ace8a6fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=5,\\,w=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection/4d66e9ee3fad00372e465398e93e2dd55a348d33e400f6282fe479e0a0ecbda3" :answer/id #uuid "9b1e6f27-62b4-5ba3-92b5-e1046ad28cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=-3,\\,w=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection/ac9d4e06a2df3b3f16a78221df4ed467126157128e69f020bb2c7d1adc9252f0" :answer/id #uuid "3ed5804a-1aae-54e2-90cf-8172a2c174fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=9,\\,w=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection/b3270ab2b259261790b7f588a407c214af7ee46eb93b2b9d87390dc93dd767e9" :answer/id #uuid "cdb91101-157d-5632-af99-cf5cc918710f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=7,\\,w=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection/ee07498c28d32ae5cf52876c56ad8c48d62b2d13f2853837ddf76c00fe0aaeb1" :answer/id #uuid "cc217f3b-7277-5dba-8522-0fa9277adb2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=2,\\,w=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "05389c48-39b0-572f-a429-50c67dc31733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216071/selection/b3270ab2b259261790b7f588a407c214af7ee46eb93b2b9d87390dc93dd767e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-216071/selection/1cdb79a815d8131b9bb3ea2d69f4bf518d6d419b61574ce7ce45e2877b717e2a" "q-216071/selection/4d66e9ee3fad00372e465398e93e2dd55a348d33e400f6282fe479e0a0ecbda3" "q-216071/selection/ac9d4e06a2df3b3f16a78221df4ed467126157128e69f020bb2c7d1adc9252f0" "q-216071/selection/b3270ab2b259261790b7f588a407c214af7ee46eb93b2b9d87390dc93dd767e9" "q-216071/selection/ee07498c28d32ae5cf52876c56ad8c48d62b2d13f2853837ddf76c00fe0aaeb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216071" :question/id #uuid "27c1063e-f4a2-5692-98c2-9ec7c68b6839" :question/math-academy-id "q-216071" :question/problem "Find the solution to the  following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}u-\\frac{1}{3}w=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}u-\\frac{1}{2}w=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $6$ and the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}u-\\frac{1}{3}w=\\frac{1}{2} & |\\times 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}u-\\frac{1}{2}w=\\frac{2}{5} & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u-2w=3 \\\\ 2u-5w=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u-2w & =3 \\\\ u & =2w+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $u=2w+3$ into the second equation and then solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u-5w & =4 \\\\ 2(2w+3)-5w & =4 \\\\ 4w+6-5w & =4 \\\\ -w+6 & =4 \\\\ -w & =-2 \\\\ w & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $u,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation $u=2w+3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2w+3 \\\\  & =2(2)+3 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $u=7$ and $w=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-216071/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
